  "level": "A1",
  "unit": 34,
  "title": "At school",
  "description": "Name the things on a school desk, and say what happens in class.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "Everything on a school desk has a name, and a school day has a shape. This unit gives you both: the objects and the words for the parts of the day.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The nouns",
        "body": "El cuaderno, el bolígrafo, el examen, el recreo y el diccionario are masculine. La mochila, la regla, la tiza, la clase y la pizarra are feminine. La clase means both the lesson and the group of people in it, and el recreo is the break between lessons.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "el cuaderno",
            "en": "the notebook"
          },
          {
            "es": "la mochila",
            "en": "the rucksack"
          },
          {
            "es": "la pizarra",
            "en": "the blackboard"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "A school day",
        "body": "The day has parts and each one is a noun: la clase, el recreo, el examen. Ser says what something is: el examen es difícil. Estar says how something is: la clase está mañana, the lesson is tomorrow.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "el examen es difícil",
            "en": "the exam is difficult"
          },
          {
            "es": "el recreo es a las once",
            "en": "the break is at eleven"
          },
          {
            "es": "la mochila está en la silla",
            "en": "the rucksack is on the chair"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
